  "derivedSlots": {
    "$comment": "Boxes NOT verbatim from the official template, with the reason. Every entry is a deliberate composition inside the official margins (x>=50, right edge <=1870); the test enforces that.",
    "three-up.title": "Title row borrowed from Tri-Fact idx27 (50,75,1820,75); 'Title & 1/3 Containers' ships only a dek row, no title.",
    "quad.title": "Same borrowed title row; '2x2 blocks' ships only a dek row.",
    "timeline.title": "Same borrowed title row; 'Timeline x4' ships only a dek row.",
    "chart-takeaway.chart": "Left column widened from the 2-Column body (885.3 -> 1180) so a chart has usable area; right column becomes the insights rail.",
    "chart-takeaway.insights": "Right rail narrowed to 590 to pair with the widened chart box; both keep the official y=275/h=690 band.",
    "full-bleed-image.image": "The official 'Photo' pic box is (0,-453.8,1920,1987.5) - deliberately oversized for pan/crop in PowerPoint. An HTML deck crops with object-fit instead, so the box is the exact canvas.",
    "full-bleed-image.caption": "No caption slot exists on 'Photo'. Placed on the brand 50px margin above the bottom safe line. Marked onImage:true so it renders on a scrim with light ink: contrast over arbitrary photo pixels cannot be computed from CSS backgrounds, and muted ink over a mid-tone image measured 1.653:1.",
    "tri-fact.value1..3": "Official Tri-Fact is asymmetric on purpose (idx1=180pt hero, idx23/idx25=72pt) and idx25 sits 12.5px lower than its peers. For three PEER metrics that asymmetry reads as a layout bug, so all three values use the 72pt tier on one baseline. Use big-fact when one number should dominate.",
    "pageNumber": "Per-layout slide-number position from the official sldNum placeholders: Agenda x=1223, Title & Bullets x=1223 (both LEFT of the full-height side image), Photo centred at x=944.4. A single hardcoded right:44px corner put the number ON the side image, where contrast is not computable. Photo's official y=1029.6 is kept at x but moved to y=988: the template's own value puts the box bottom at 1059.5, 23.5px past the 1036 safe line, and copying that would force us to suppress our own margin rule."
  },
